The plate looks like a side or dinner plate of roughly 22-26 cm. The two rib sections are each about 13-15 cm long and 3-4 cm wide, which suggests small portions of pork ribs, probably 3-4 bones each.

I'd put each section at about 70-80 g including bone, so roughly 150 g in total. Bone makes up about 35% of that, leaving around 100 g of edible meat. Glazed pork spare ribs run about 250-300 kcal per 100 g of edible meat. Roughly 100 g of meat plus glaze comes to about 280 kcal.

